# oracle: cut-down of examples/PACKAGES/mesont/in.film_mesocnt: four CNT chains (molecules 1, 81, 93, 84 of data.film_mesocnt: 804 atoms, the closest chains of the film) with bond_style mesocnt, angle_style mesocnt (buckling) and pair_style mesocnt 40 chain id, 50 steps of NVT at 300 K (the example's boundary p p s, special_bonds lj 1 1 1, timestep 0.01 ps). Native: installed lmp (MESONT, commit b332f28). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box) against the engine: the thermo rows agree to 7e-12 relative (the per-atom energy checksums c_chka, c_chkb, the largest at 7e-12); the per-atom x, v, f agree to 2.7e-10 relative (max 1.2e-10 absolute, atom 659 fy, after 50 MD steps; fixture regenerated with the coarse potential); the tolerance below is the 1e-8 target. Potential: tests/oracle/w157mt_C_10_10_coarse.mesocnt, derived from potentials/C_10_10.mesocnt (sha256 923f600a081d948eb8b4510f84aa96167b5a6c3e1aba16845d2364ae137dc346) by keeping every 20th grid point of its 1001-point axes (both ends kept, the ranges unchanged), because the full 86 MB file cannot go in the repository.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8
# oracle-inputs: w157mt_film.data w157mt_C_10_10_coarse.mesocnt
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p s
atom_style full
special_bonds lj 1 1 1
newton on
read_data w157mt_film.data
bond_style mesocnt
bond_coeff 1 C 10 10 10
angle_style mesocnt
angle_coeff 1 buckling C 10 10 10
pair_style mesocnt 40 chain id
pair_coeff * * w157mt_C_10_10_coarse.mesocnt 1
fix angle_mesocnt_buckled all property/atom i_buckled ghost yes
compute epa all pe/atom pair
compute epb all pe/atom angle bond
variable wpa atom c_epa*id*sin(id)
variable wpb atom c_epb*id*cos(id)
compute chka all reduce sum v_wpa
compute chkb all reduce sum v_wpb
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal ebond eangle epair c_chka c_chkb
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run 0
velocity all create 600.0 2022 loop geom
timestep 0.01
fix nvt all nvt temp 300.0 300.0 1
run 50
